---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/contact-form.css';
import '../styles/testimonials.css';
---
<Layout title="Afterglow Automations — AI Command Centers for Event Businesses" description="Custom AI command centers, workflow automation, content and SEO systems, and Google Ads management for event businesses.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-kicker"><span></span> AI command centers for event businesses</div>
    <h1>One command center.<br/><i>Your whole</i> <span class="glow-word">business.</span></h1>
    <div class="hero-bottom">
      <p>Connect your CRM, marketing, SEO, content, leads, revenue, and operations—then automate what happens next.</p>
      <a class="circle-link" href="#work" aria-label="See the work"><span>SEE<br/>THE WORK</span><b>↓</b></a>
    </div>
    <div class="light-streak streak-one"></div><div class="light-streak streak-two"></div>
    <div class="hero-stamp">BUILT BY SOMEONE<br/>WHO BUILT AN<br/>EVENT BUSINESS <span>✦</span></div>
  </section>

  <div class="marquee" aria-label="Services"><div>ONE COMMAND CENTER <i>✦</i> CONTENT + SEO AUTOMATED <i>✦</i> GOOGLE ADS MANAGED <i>✦</i> EVERY SYSTEM CONNECTED <i>✦</i> NEXT MOVES AUTOMATED <i>✦</i> ONE COMMAND CENTER <i>✦</i> CONTENT + SEO AUTOMATED <i>✦</i> GOOGLE ADS MANAGED <i>✦</i></div></div>

  <section class="intro reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">THE BUSINESS BEHIND THE PARTY</p>
    <div><h2>Your events are electric.<br/>Your operations should be, too.</h2><p>Most event businesses are held together by a CRM, spreadsheets, inboxes, text threads, and an owner who remembers everything. Afterglow connects those pieces into one clear operating picture—so you can stop reconstructing the business every morning and start acting on what matters.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="command-center reveal" aria-labelledby="command-title">
    <div class="command-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">THIS ISN’T ANOTHER REPORTING DASHBOARD</p>
      <h2 id="command-title">One operating layer.<br/><i>Built to take action.</i></h2>
      <p>Keep your CRM. Keep the tools your team already knows. I build the automated layer above them—bringing the right signals into one place, showing you what needs attention, and triggering the work that should happen next.</p>
      <a href="#contact">Map my command center <span>↗</span></a>
    </div>
    <div class="system-map" aria-label="Connected event business command center diagram">
      <div class="system-node node-honeybook"><b>Your CRM</b><span>Leads · Projects · Payments</span></div>
      <div class="system-node node-gsc"><b>Search Console</b><span>Queries · Pages · Rankings</span></div>
      <div class="system-node node-ga"><b>Google Analytics</b><span>Traffic · Journeys · Conversion</span></div>
      <div class="system-node node-content"><b>Content engine</b><span>Plan · Create · Publish · Track</span></div>
      <div class="system-node node-seo"><b>SEO tracker</b><span>Visibility · Leads · Revenue</span></div>
      <div class="system-node node-smart"><b>Google Ads</b><span>Campaigns · Spend · Conversions</span></div>
      <div class="system-core"><span>LIVE OWNER VIEW</span><strong>What needs<br/>attention now?</strong><small>Updated automatically</small></div>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 700 570" role="presentation" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M195 82 C300 100 293 211 352 280"/><path d="M505 82 C400 100 408 205 352 280"/><path d="M155 280 C235 280 267 280 352 280"/><path d="M545 280 C470 280 435 280 352 280"/><path d="M196 485 C285 430 291 345 352 280"/><path d="M504 485 C415 430 414 344 352 280"/></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-cloud" aria-label="Additional tools that can connect to the command center">
      <span class="tool-cloud-label">AND THE TOOLS EVENT BUSINESSES ALREADY LIVE IN</span>
      <div class="tool-groups">
        <div class="tool-group"><b>BOOKINGS + CRM</b><div><span>Check Cherry</span><span>BoothBook</span><span>Dubsado</span><span>17hats</span><span>Táve</span><span>GoHighLevel</span></div></div>
        <div class="tool-group"><b>PLANNING + RENTALS</b><div><span>Aisle Planner</span><span>Planning Pod</span><span>Tripleseat</span><span>Goodshuffle Pro</span><span>Booqable</span><span>Google Calendar</span></div></div>
        <div class="tool-group"><b>MONEY + TEAM</b><div><span>QuickBooks</span><span>Stripe</span><span>Square</span><span>When I Work</span><span>Slack</span></div></div>
        <div class="tool-group"><b>GROWTH + COMMUNICATIONS</b><div><span>Smartlead</span><span>Meta Ads</span><span>Mailchimp</span><span>Gmail</span><span>Calendly</span><span>Twilio</span><span>Website forms</span></div></div>
        <div class="tool-group"><b>DATA + AUTOMATION</b><div><span>Zapier</span><span>Make</span><span>Google Sheets</span><span>Airtable</span><strong>+ anything with an API</strong></div></div>
      </div>
      <small>Connected through direct APIs, supported automations, or structured imports—depending on the platform.</small>
    </div>
    <div class="outcome-strip outcome-three">
      <div><span>01 / SEE</span><b>See everything</b><p>Leads, bookings, payments, SEO, content, staffing, and upcoming events in one owner view.</p></div>
      <div><span>02 / KNOW</span><b>Know what matters</b><p>Overdue follow-ups, missed opportunities, busy dates, falling rankings, and unpaid balances surface early.</p></div>
      <div><span>03 / AUTOMATE</span><b>Move without chasing</b><p>Trigger follow-up, reporting, content workflows, reminders, synchronization, and owner alerts.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="work" class="work-section">
    <div class="section-heading reveal"><p class="eyebrow">PROOF, NOT PITCHES</p><h2>Built for the<br/><i>real world.</i></h2><span>01 — 03</span></div>
    <article class="case case-feature reveal">
      <div class="case-copy"><p class="case-number">01 / ZIM ZOOM</p><h3>From operational guesswork to one clear command center.</h3><p>Events, equipment capacity, staffing, payments, metrics, and Slack approvals were spread across separate systems. I brought them together in a secure owner view built around one question: what needs attention today?</p><div class="stats"><div><strong>7–16</strong><span>hours projected back every week</span></div><div><strong>1</strong><span>operating picture</span></div></div><a href="/work/zim-zoom">See the case study <span>↗</span></a></div>
      <a href="/work/zim-zoom" class="case-image pink-frame"><img src="/images/zimzoom-dashboard.png" alt="Zim Zoom operations command center owner dashboard" loading="lazy"/><span class="image-label">THE OWNER VIEW</span></a>
    </article>
    <article class="case case-reverse reveal">
      <div class="case-copy"><p class="case-number">02 / SOUTHERN REVELRY</p><h3>Leads, revenue, ads, and SEO—finally telling the same story.</h3><p>CRM data, Google Sheets, Ads, Search Console, and follow-up workflows became one operating layer for a multi-service Texas event company.</p><ul><li>Clear next step for every lead</li><li>Closed-loop marketing visibility</li><li>Source truth stays intact</li></ul><a href="/work/southern-revelry">See the case study <span>↗</span></a></div>
          <a href="/work/southern-revelry" class="case-image lime-frame"><img src="/images/southern-dashboard.png" alt="Southern Revelry revenue and operations command center" loading="lazy"/><span class="image-label">REVENUE + OPERATIONS</span></a>
    </article>
    <article class="case popstar reveal">
      <div><img src="/images/popstar-site.png" alt="Popstar Photo Booths website" loading="lazy"/></div>
      <div class="case-copy"><p class="case-number">03 / POPSTAR</p><h3>I didn’t just advise event businesses. I built one, grew it with SEO, and sold it.</h3><p>That owner’s perspective changes the work. I know the difference between a clever technology demo and a system that actually earns its keep during a packed event weekend.</p><div class="owned-stamp">BUILT <span>→</span> RANKED <span>→</span> SOLD</div></div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="testimonials-section" aria-labelledby="testimonials-title">
    <div class="testimonials-heading reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">FROM THE PEOPLE IN IT</p>
      <h2 id="testimonials-title">Built around the way<br/><i>event businesses actually run.</i></h2>
      <p>The systems are custom. The result is recognizable: less chasing, clearer numbers, and more room to lead the business.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="testimonial-grid">
      <article class="testimonial-card testimonial-lime reveal">
        <div class="testimonial-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</div>
        <blockquote>Danny connected our CRM, Google Sheets, Google Ads, Search Console, and follow-up workflow into one command center. It saves us hours of manual reporting and follow-up every week, helps us cut wasted ad spend, and makes it easier to protect revenue by showing exactly where leads and opportunities are getting stuck.</blockquote>
        <footer class="testimonial-person">
          <img class="testimonial-avatar testimonial-avatar-image" src="/images/justin-goss-southern-revelry.jpg" alt="Justin Goss from Southern Revelry" width="400" height="400" loading="lazy" />
          <div><strong>Justin Goss</strong><span>Southern Revelry</span></div>
        </footer>
      </article>
      <article class="testimonial-card testimonial-pink reveal">
        <div class="testimonial-mark" aria-hidden="true">“</div>
        <blockquote>Danny connected our booking data, metrics, Slack approvals, staffing, capacity, and payments into one owner view. We project saving 7–16 hours every week—roughly 350–800 hours a year—while catching past-due balances and capacity risks before they cost us.</blockquote>
        <footer class="testimonial-person">
          <img class="testimonial-avatar testimonial-avatar-image" src="/images/sushma-zim-zoom.jpg" alt="Sushma from Zim Zoom Photo Booth" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy" />
          <div><strong>Sushma</strong><span>Zim Zoom Photo Booth</span></div>
        </footer>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="services" class="services">
    <div class="section-heading reveal"><p class="eyebrow">WHAT YOUR COMMAND CENTER CAN RUN</p><h2>Less chasing.<br/><i>More momentum.</i></h2></div>
    <div class="service-grid reveal">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Sales + follow-up</h3><p>Capture inquiries, surface response gaps, track proposals, prioritize hot leads, automate reminders, and see exactly where bookings stall.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Content + SEO</h3><p>Turn Search Console data into content plans, automated briefs, publishing workflows, refresh queues, and clear tracking from rankings to inquiries.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Google Ads + growth</h3><p>Campaign management, conversion tracking, budget pacing, search-term reviews, performance alerts, and automation tied to qualified leads and booked revenue.</p></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Events + operations</h3><p>See capacity, staffing, equipment, payments, upcoming events, decisions, and integration health before small issues become event-day problems.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="process" class="process-section">
    <div class="process-intro reveal"><p class="eyebrow">START USEFUL. THEN EXPAND.</p><h2>You don’t have to rebuild<br/><i>everything at once.</i></h2><p>We start with the bottleneck costing you the most time or money, build the first useful owner view, and connect more of the business from there.</p></div>
    <div class="process-steps reveal">
      <article><span>WEEK 01</span><div><h3>Map the moving parts</h3><p>We trace the real workflow, identify where information breaks down, and choose the highest-value first release.</p></div></article>
      <article><span>BUILD</span><div><h3>Launch the first useful view</h3><p>I connect the essential systems, build your command center, and automate the first set of clear next actions.</p></div></article>
      <article><span>EXPAND</span><div><h3>Keep compounding</h3><p>Add marketing attribution, content automation, finance, staffing, or other workflows as the foundation proves its value.</p></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-section">
    <div class="faq-heading reveal"><p class="eyebrow">GOOD QUESTIONS</p><h2>Before we<br/><i>connect the dots.</i></h2></div>
    <div class="faq-list reveal">
      <details><summary>Does this replace my CRM?</summary><p>Usually, no. Your CRM can remain the system your team uses every day. Afterglow connects it with the marketing, reporting, operational, and follow-up tools around it—then adds the automation and owner visibility those systems are missing.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do I need perfectly clean data first?</summary><p>No. Real businesses rarely have perfect data. I preserve the source, make uncertainty visible, and build review steps where an automated guess could create problems.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What kinds of event businesses do you work with?</summary><p>I work with planners, entertainment companies, rental and production teams, venues, caterers, experiential businesses, and other operators who need their sales, marketing, and delivery systems to work together.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What can actually be automated?</summary><p>Lead routing, follow-up reminders, owner alerts, reporting, content and SEO workflows, Google Ads monitoring, data synchronization, payment-risk flags, staffing queues, and more. The exact system is shaped around your operation.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will I still control the business?</summary><p>Yes. Important decisions remain visible and reversible. You get clear ownership, source tracking, safeguards, and human approval wherever automation should assist rather than decide.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="about" class="about reveal">
    <div class="portrait"><img src="/images/danny.jpg" alt="Danny Sullivan, founder of Afterglow Automations" loading="lazy"/><span>YOUR AI PERSON<br/>FOR EVENT PEOPLE</span></div>
    <div><p class="eyebrow">HI, I’M DANNY</p><h2>I build AI products.<br/><i>I’ve run an event business.</i></h2><div class="current-role"><div class="gametime-logo"><img src="/images/gametime.jpg" alt="Gametime" loading="lazy"/></div><div><span>CURRENT ROLE</span><strong>AI Product Engineer · Gametime</strong><p>I build production AI systems for live-event discovery and venue imagery, with millions of dollars in GMV riding on their reliability.</p></div></div><p>I’ve also created 28 technology courses and labs for Pluralsight, worked in growth marketing at Stash, and taught software development at Flatiron School.</p><p>Before that, I built and sold my own event company, growing it through SEO and operating it through real event weekends. Afterglow brings those two sides of my career together: serious AI product work and firsthand event-business experience.</p><p>You work directly with me from the first conversation through the finished system.</p><div class="credentials"><span>AI PRODUCT ENGINEER · GAMETIME</span><span>28 PLURALSIGHT COURSES + LABS</span><span>GROWTH · STASH</span><span>EDUCATOR · FLATIRON SCHOOL</span><span>EVENT COMPANY FOUNDER</span></div><a class="bio-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/danny-sullivan-raleigh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Connect with me on LinkedIn <span>↗</span></a></div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="contact">
    <div class="contact-star">✦</div>
    <div class="contact-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">YOUR MOVE</p>
      <h2>What’s stealing time<br/>from your <i>best work?</i></h2>
      <p>Tell me the workflow, bottleneck, or growth goal you keep thinking about. I’ll give you an honest read on where AI—or simpler software—can help.</p>
    </div>
    <form class="contact-form" name="event-business-inquiry" method="POST" action="/thanks/" data-netlify="true" netlify-honeypot="bot-field">
      <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="event-business-inquiry" />
      <p class="form-honeypot"><label>Don’t fill this out if you’re human: <input name="bot-field" /></label></p>
      <div class="form-grid">
        <label>
          <span>Your name *</span>
          <input type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" required placeholder="Your name" />
        </label>
        <label>
          <span>Email *</span>
          <input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required placeholder="you@company.com" />
        </label>
        <label>
          <span>Company *</span>
          <input type="text" name="company" autocomplete="organization" required placeholder="Your event business" />
        </label>
        <label>
          <span>Type of business</span>
          <select name="business-type">
            <option value="">Choose one</option>
            <option>Experiential or activation company</option>
            <option>Wedding or event planner</option>
            <option>DJ or entertainment company</option>
            <option>Venue or catering company</option>
            <option>Rental company</option>
            <option>Other event business</option>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label class="form-wide">
          <span>Website</span>
          <input type="url" name="website" autocomplete="url" placeholder="https://" />
        </label>
        <label class="form-wide">
          <span>What would you like to fix or automate? *</span>
          <textarea name="message" rows="5" required placeholder="Tell me what’s taking too much time, where leads get lost, or what you wish you could see in one place."></textarea>
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="form-footer">
        <button type="submit">SEND MY DETAILS <span>↗</span></button>
        <p>No sales maze. Danny reads every message and replies personally.</p>
      </div>
    </form>
    <small>Prefer email? <a href="mailto:danny@afterglowautomations.com?subject=Let’s talk about my event business">danny@afterglowautomations.com</a></small>
  </section>
</Layout>
